  "question": {
    "text": "Let $e_1$ and $e_2$ be the eccentricities of the ellipse $\\frac{\\mathrm{x}^2}{\\mathrm{~b}^2}+\\frac{\\mathrm{y}^2}{25}=1 \\quad$ and the hyperbola $\\quad \\frac{\\mathrm{x}^2}{16}-\\frac{\\mathrm{y}^2}{\\mathrm{~b}^2}=1$, respectively. If $\\mathrm{b} \\lt 5$ and $\\mathrm{e}_1 \\mathrm{e}_2=1$, then the eccentricity of the ellipse having its axes along the coordinate axes and passing through all four foci (two of the ellipse and two of the hyperbola) is :"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{4}{5}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{3}{5}$",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{4}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{aligned}<br/>& \\mathrm{e}_1^2=1-\\frac{\\mathrm{b}^2}{25} \\quad \\mathrm{e}_2^2=1-\\frac{\\mathrm{b}^2}{16} \\\\\n& \\therefore \\mathrm{e}_1^2 \\mathrm{e}_2^2=1 \\\\\n& \\left(1-\\frac{\\mathrm{b}^2}{25}\\right)\\left(1+\\frac{\\mathrm{b}^2}{16}\\right)=1 \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow 2+\\frac{\\mathrm{b}^2}{16}-\\frac{\\mathrm{b}^2}{25}-\\frac{\\mathrm{b}^2}{400}=1 \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow \\frac{9 \\mathrm{~b}^2}{400}=\\frac{\\mathrm{b}^4}{400} \\\\\n& \\mathrm{~b}^2=9 \\\\\n& \\frac{\\mathrm{x}^2}{9}+\\frac{\\mathrm{y}^2}{25}=1 \\quad \\frac{\\mathrm{x}^2}{16}-\\frac{\\mathrm{y}^2}{9}=0 \\\\\n& \\mathrm{e}_1 \\sqrt{1-\\frac{9}{25}} \\\\\n& \\mathrm{e}_1=\\frac{4}{5}<br/>\\end{aligned}$<br/>Focii : - $(0, \\pm 4) \\quad( \\pm 5,0)$<br/>ellipse passing through all four foci<br/>$\\begin{aligned}<br/>& \\frac{x^2}{25}+\\frac{y^2}{16}=1 \\\\\n& e=\\sqrt{1-\\frac{16}{25}}=\\frac{3}{5}<br/>\\end{aligned}$"
  }
